/*
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
    UIShrine.uss
    Shrine Feedback  —  Structure & Layout only
    Unity UIToolkit  (Unity 6.x LTS)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

    NO colors or fonts here — those live in FishMMO-Theme.uss.

    LOAD ORDER in UXML (required):
        <ui:Style src="FishMMO-Theme.uss" />
        <ui:Style src="UIShrine.uss" />

    Sized against the 1200x800 reference resolution declared by
    Assets/UI Toolkit/PanelSettings.asset.

    Non-interactive, like the gathering bar, but it does carry a
    surface (fish-well). Unlike the gathering bar it is nothing but
    text, and text floating directly over the 3D world is legible
    only against whatever happens to be behind it — which for a
    shrine is usually bright particle effects.

    Its whole job is to answer a keypress that would otherwise look
    ignored: a shrine on cooldown refuses silently on the server,
    and a refusal the player cannot see is indistinguishable from
    a dropped packet.

    The text authored in the UXML is placeholder. The panel starts
    closed and every open writes both labels before it is shown, so
    the placeholder is never on screen — it exists so the panel
    renders as something in the editor preview rather than as an
    empty rectangle.
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
*/

/* Above centre so it does not sit under the crosshair, and well clear of the gathering bar
   below it — the two can legitimately be on screen at once. */
.shrine-panel {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%; top: 34%; translate: -50% -50%;
    width: 280px;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 8px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    padding-left: 12px;
    padding-right: 12px;
}

.shrine-title {
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.shrine-message {
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    margin-top: 2px;
    white-space: normal;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
